# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is gitignored and is
# loaded automatically by the lifecycle wrapper (scripts/toolbox-run.sh) and
# by the mise tasks (see mise.toml [settings] env_file = ".env").
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The local-host environment needs no cloud credentials and no plaintext
# secrets: the single kind cluster is self-contained and syncs from an OCI
# artifact that the bootstrap publishes from this checkout. Credentials enter
# the tree only as SOPS-encrypted *.sops.yaml manifests under workload/ (see
# docs/secrets.md); the age private key stays local in age.agekey (gitignored).

# ── Container engine (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# toolbox-run.sh auto-detects Docker or Podman. Set this to force one:
# CONTAINER_ENGINE="podman"

# ── Not settable here (toolbox-computed) ──────────────────────────────────────
# ENGINE_SOCK and KUBECONFIG are always computed by scripts/toolbox-run.sh on
# every run; a value for either of them in this file is loaded into the shell
# but then unconditionally overwritten before the container starts, so it has
# no effect. See docs/operations.md ("Toolbox container").

# ── Other lifecycle knobs (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# KAIPR_PROFILE, REGISTRY_PORT, REGISTRY_READY_RETRIES,
# LOCAL_RECONCILE_TIMEOUT, KAIPR_KUBECONFIG, and
# OCI_REPOSITORY/OCI_TAG are operator-settable here; see the table in
# docs/bootstrap-cli.md ("Bootstrap controls") for defaults instead of
# duplicating it here.

# ── Notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# • NEVER commit .env or any file containing real credentials
